(1. The Staged Continuum Paradigm) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(The continuum model of tendon pathology differentiates load-induced presentation into three continuous stages:) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(• Reactive Tendinopathy: Acute, non-inflammatory cellular response to tensile or compressive load spike.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(• Tendon Disrepair: Focal matrix disruption, chondrocytic cell proliferation, and capillary ingrowth.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(• Degenerative Tendinopathy: Disorganized collagen matrix with large areas of cell death and minimal repair capacity.) Tj
0 -18 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(2. Clinical Load Management & Treatment Strategies) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(• Reactive stage priority: Load management. Reduce high-tensile energy-storage activities \(jumping, sprinting\).) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(• Isometric holds \(5 x 45 seconds at 70% MVC\) produce immediate cortical inhibition and reliable analgesic relief.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(• Heavy Slow Resistance \(HSR\) training \(3 x weekly, 3-4 sets of 6-8 RM\) promotes positive collagen mechanical adaptation.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 8.5 Tf
(• Energy storage and release training must be reintroduced progressively before return-to-sport clearance.) Tj
0 -24 Td
/F1 7.5 Tf
